A||N||8||HYPTNOTiSE||Performance guys L@@K! Hi-Po harmonic balancer||||1||
Z||000000||HYPTNOTiSE||12-03-2000||01:45 PM||||I was looking through summit racings catalog, and it sparked an interest.  I want a fluid dampner harmonic balaner.  The stock balancer isn't going to be really good for my application, i'm going to be reving high like 6700-7000 often. I just dont trust the stock balancer for that. So i want to go with a fluid dampner, which is like 150 bucks for SBC internally balanced?  Has anyone ever retro fitted one?  they're would be a few things needed, but they list an application for 90 degree v-6.  Our crank pulley is held on by 4 bolts if i remember correctly and the SBC pulley is held on by 3. So either i'd have to drill new holes in the crank pulley, or in the harmonic balancer. I wonder if they keyways and the crank end size are alike?          <BR> Any info would really be appreciated!<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||12-03-2000||09:25 PM||||just an idea but you could re-drill <BR>the holes in the new balancer then machine a large plate like 2-3" in diameter to help reinforce the balancers swiss cheese looking flange.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||12-03-2000||10:42 PM||||The stock damper is plenty adequate for your 2.8-liter engine. You’re just wasting $150 and making someone else rich because they made an ad that convinced you to buy one. Don’t do it!||||reg||1
Z||000003||RNGCRSH||12-03-2000||11:12 PM||||Factory harmonic balancers are no good for high performance engines. They are designed for normal street use. For high reving engines you want to make sure its a captive design. This means the outer ring can't come seperated from the inner hub.<BR>  I lost a ballancer on my Drag car. it was easy to fix also. All I had to do was replace the radiator,water pump, fan, and the block. its amazing what a 10 lb chunk of steel can do at 8000 RPM.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||12-04-2000||01:01 AM||||My God, whatever you do, don't rev your 2.8L to 8000 rpm wihtout a hipo blanacer! THINK OF THE CHILDREN!<P>I'd save my money....<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000005||loafer87gt||12-04-2000||10:49 AM||||Err, can someone tell the idiot here what a hi-po dampener is. I thought a harmonic dampener was something on a Automatic transmission?||||reg||1
Z||000006||HYPTNOTiSE||12-04-2000||12:13 PM||||I really dont think that 150 dollars is a waste of money. Factory harmonic balancers are no good for race engines. Also my 3.2 L engine has been precision balanced, and i want to insure that it stays balanced at all rpms. The thing that i like about the fluid dampner is that it changes how it's balanced all the time. It's not fixed at one set balance. Also i had a similar thing happen to me, i lost the outter ring on my stock harmonic balancer on my fiero. It took all the belts off with it and smashed up the oil pan. So i had an over heating, oil leaking p.o.s. laying in the middle of the road. No thanks,dont want that to happen again. especially not at 7K rpm so peices come through the back window or up through the decklid. <P>Loafer the harmonic balancer goes on the front of the engine on the crank shaft.  Same place where your crank pulley bolts up. They're on all engines. <p>[This message has been edited by HYPTNOTiSE (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||12-04-2000||12:31 PM||||A harmonic balancer helps reduce the torsional resonances in the crankshaft. The crankshaft has a little spring to it, and every time a cylinder fires it is twisting that springiness against the load of the transmission. This sets up a torsional oscillation that is bad for things. A harmonic balancer is basically a torsional oscillator that is tuned to break up the torsional resonance in the crankshaft.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||12-04-2000||12:56 PM||||Wouldn't you want to balance the motor <B>with</B> the hypo SFI balancer attached, even tho its internally balanced?<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
